# Host-layer headers (#27, delivery.md §2.1/§2.3, agent-surface.md §5.1/§5.3).
#
# Cloudflare Workers static assets read this file from the asset directory, so it is authored
# under `public/` and ships as `dist/_headers` — it is a rule file, never served as an asset.
# A request inherits every matching rule, and a header set twice is joined with a comma, so
# `scripts/check-platform.mjs` holds this file to the five entries the spec fixes and refuses
# two overlapping rules that set one name.

/*.md
	Content-Type: text/markdown; charset=utf-8

# The platform's default MIME for `.md` and `.txt` is unmeasured (delivery.md §10.2), so both
# overrides are unconditional: `/llms.txt` is a plain-text file and says so.
/llms.txt
	Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

# Fingerprinted build assets never change under their name (delivery.md §2.4). HTML is left on
# the platform default (`must-revalidate` + ETag) so a content change is visible immediately.
/_astro/*
	Cache-Control: public, max-age=31556952, immutable

# Agent-surface discovery, site-wide (agent-surface.md §5.3): `Link` is the llmstxt.org
# discovery shape, `X-Llms-Txt` the de-facto header every llms.txt-aware crawler reads.
/*
	Link: </llms.txt>; rel="llms-txt"
	X-Llms-Txt: /llms.txt
